# STIG AS24-U1-000680: The Apache web server must be configured to immediately disconnect or disable re
# STIG ID: V-214260 (MEDIUM)

META
    esp_id `apache-as24-u1-000680-disconnect-config-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `apache`
    criticality `high`
    title `STIG AS24-U1-000680: The Apache web server must be configured to immediately disconnect or disable re`
    description `The Apache web server must be configured to immediately disconnect or disable re`
    author `example-security`
    tags `apache,stig,disa-stig`
    control_mapping `DISA-STIG:AS24-U1-000680,NIST-800-53:AC-17(9)`
    control_objective `AC-17(9)`
    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`
    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Apache:localhost:web-hardening`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`
    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Review and remediate per DISA Apache STIG guidance for AS24-U1-000680.`
    component_id `comp-apache-web`
META_END

DEF
    VAR config_path string `/etc/httpd/conf/httpd.conf`

    OBJECT httpd_config
        path VAR config_path
    OBJECT_END

    STATE config_check
        content string contains `MaxKeepAliveRequests`
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN file_content
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF config_check
            OBJECT_REF httpd_config
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
